If I can’t start pronouncing this now,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:28.520 --> 00:02:34.520
it’s going to be a long webinar:&nbsp;
nicotinamide adenine dinucleotide,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:34.520 --> 00:02:38.480
which is an essential cofactor for&nbsp;
hundreds of enzymes within the body,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:38.480 --> 00:02:49.080
including a purported anti-aging enzyme. Raising&nbsp;
levels can extend lifespan and rejuvenate&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:49.080 --> 00:02:54.360
health in a variety of animals. What about in&nbsp;
humans? That’s what we’re going to talk about.

00:02:54.360 --> 00:02:59.920
The four main NAD-boosting supplements&nbsp;
on the market are nicotinamide riboside,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:59.920 --> 00:03:07.280
also known as NR; nicotinamide mononucleotide,&nbsp;
also known as NMN; nicotinic acid;&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:07.280 --> 00:03:13.720
and nicotinamide. In this two-hour webinar, I&nbsp;
will cover the pros and cons of each of those,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:13.720 --> 00:03:18.880
as well as the other five NAD-boosting&nbsp;
supplements on the market. I’ll also&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:18.880 --> 00:03:25.640
discuss three ways to naturally boost NAD&nbsp;
levels without taking any supplements at all.

00:03:25.640 --> 00:03:29.880
Let’s begin with a video that&nbsp;
lays out what exactly NAD&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:29.880 --> 00:03:43.680
is and asks the question: do&nbsp;
NAD levels decline with age?

00:03:48.840 --> 00:03:53.920
Our understanding of nicotinamide
adenine dinucleotide (NAD+)

00:03:53.920 --> 00:03:59.080
arose from humble beginnings as a factor
noted to enhance yeast fermentation

00:03:59.080 --> 00:04:05.600
in a 1906 paper unassumingly entitled
“The Alcoholic Ferment of Yeast-Juice.”

00:04:05.600 --> 00:04:08.920
Little did they know that
waves of NAD-related discoveries

00:04:08.920 --> 00:04:12.360
would go on to yield a
total of four Nobel Prizes.

00:04:12.360 --> 00:04:16.920
NAD+ is now known as an essential
molecule for all living organisms,

00:04:16.920 --> 00:04:19.880
required for the function
of about 500 enzymes,

00:04:19.880 --> 00:04:24.400
including, notably, the extraction
of metabolic energy from food.

00:04:24.400 --> 00:04:28.760
The 21st century has produced yet
another scientific renaissance for NAD+

00:04:28.760 --> 00:04:32.440
with the realization that it was
critical for the activity of sirtuins,

00:04:32.440 --> 00:04:38.320
the “guardians of mammalian healthspan”
I detail in my book, How Not to Age.

00:04:38.320 --> 00:04:42.320
NAD+ is one of the most abundant
molecules in our body.

00:04:42.320 --> 00:04:44.000
Once considered relatively stable,

00:04:44.000 --> 00:04:49.080
it’s now known to be in a constant state
of synthesis, recycling, and breakdown.

00:04:49.080 --> 00:04:51.560
The entire pool of NAD+
in some of our tissues

00:04:51.560 --> 00:04:55.080
is turned over
several times a day.

00:04:55.080 --> 00:04:58.360
To maintain cellular vitality
in the face of this turnover,

00:04:58.360 --> 00:05:01.400
an adequate supply
of NAD+ precursors

00:05:01.400 --> 00:05:06.360
and sufficiently high enzyme activity
synthesizing NAD+ are critical.

00:05:06.360 --> 00:05:10.640
The importance of NAD+ is exemplified
by the devastating consequences

00:05:10.640 --> 00:05:15.080
of a deficiency of NAD+ precursors
like niacin (vitamin B3).

00:05:15.080 --> 00:05:17.520
The deficiency syndrome,
called pellagra,

00:05:17.520 --> 00:05:20.200
is characterized by the 4 D’s:

00:05:20.200 --> 00:05:25.440
dermatitis, dementia, diarrhea,
and, eventually, death.

00:05:25.440 --> 00:05:28.680
Thankfully, since life as we know
it couldn’t exist without it,

00:05:28.680 --> 00:05:32.320
NAD+ and its precursors are
found in everything we eat—

00:05:32.320 --> 00:05:34.760
plant, animal, or fungi—

00:05:34.760 --> 00:05:36.400
but we need to know
how to get at them.

00:05:36.400 --> 00:05:40.000
The niacin in corn, for instance,
is tightly bound up,

00:05:40.000 --> 00:05:44.080
but it can be released by pre-
soaking in alkaline lime-water.

00:05:44.080 --> 00:05:46.360
Maize was exported
from Latin America

00:05:46.360 --> 00:05:49.640
to become a dietary staple
without the requisite knowledge

00:05:49.640 --> 00:05:52.120
about traditional processing
techniques, though,

00:05:52.120 --> 00:05:54.960
and an epidemic
of pellagra ensued.

00:05:54.960 --> 00:05:58.720
An estimated 100,000 Americans
died from pellagra

00:05:58.720 --> 00:06:00.960
in the first few decades
of the 20th century

00:06:00.960 --> 00:06:05.360
before bread started to be
fortified with niacin in 1938.

00:06:05.360 --> 00:06:10.840
The pitch for NAD+ boosting as an
anti-aging strategy goes as follows:

00:06:10.840 --> 00:06:13.040
all species,
including humans,

00:06:13.040 --> 00:06:16.160
naturally experience a decline
in NAD+ levels over time,

00:06:16.160 --> 00:06:17.440
and this decline is, in fact,

00:06:17.440 --> 00:06:20.240
one of the major
reasons organisms age.

00:06:20.240 --> 00:06:23.000
By restoring youthful levels,
the argument goes,

00:06:23.000 --> 00:06:27.200
these age-related disorders can
be delayed or even reversed.

00:06:27.200 --> 00:06:30.240
Two leaders in the field,
one from Harvard and the other MIT,

00:06:30.240 --> 00:06:33.040
have said, respectively,
that NAD+ boosters may

00:06:33.040 --> 00:06:36.040
“hold the promise of increasing
the body’s resilience,

00:06:36.040 --> 00:06:38.520
not just to one disease,
but to many,

00:06:38.520 --> 00:06:42.000
thereby extending healthy
human lifespan,”

00:06:42.000 --> 00:06:45.400
and that sirtuin activation
by NAD+ repletion

00:06:45.400 --> 00:06:50.160
“may be the most actionable item
to emerge from aging research.”

00:06:50.160 --> 00:06:52.440
Of course, they have
both been involved

00:06:52.440 --> 00:06:56.760
in multimillion-dollar dietary
supplement companies.

00:06:56.760 --> 00:07:00.840
The first premise, that NAD+
levels decline with age,

00:07:00.840 --> 00:07:02.400
has been called into question.

00:07:02.400 --> 00:07:04.960
For example,
this 2022 review

00:07:04.960 --> 00:07:11.400
“Age-Dependent Decline of NAD+—
Universal Truth or Confounded Consensus?”

00:07:11.400 --> 00:07:16.240
concluded that, despite
systemic claims to the contrary,

00:07:16.240 --> 00:07:19.280
the evidence supporting
the premise is very limited.

00:07:19.280 --> 00:07:22.000
Indeed, the most
comprehensive study to date

00:07:22.000 --> 00:07:24.400
found significant changes
in NAD+ levels

00:07:24.400 --> 00:07:28.840
in less than half of the tested
tissues in old versus young mice.

00:07:28.840 --> 00:07:32.520
The human data are
similarly inconsistent.

00:07:32.520 --> 00:07:36.280
NAD+ boosting supplement
shills make claims like

00:07:36.280 --> 00:07:38.000
“By middle age,
our NAD+ levels

00:07:38.000 --> 00:07:40.720
have plummeted to half
that of our youth,”

00:07:40.720 --> 00:07:46.640
but the cited source only shows a
drop (in brain levels) of about 13%

00:07:46.640 --> 00:07:49.320
between about
the ages 20 to 60.

00:07:49.320 --> 00:07:54.680
A similar study estimated about
an 18% drop from age 25 to 70,

00:07:54.680 --> 00:07:59.800
both broadly consistent with a
14% drop in spinal tap fluid samples

00:07:59.800 --> 00:08:03.720
taken from those over
age 45 (average age 71),

00:08:03.720 --> 00:08:07.320
compared to those under
age 45 (average age 34).

00:08:07.320 --> 00:08:11.680
It’s unclear if such modest differences
would have any consequences,

00:08:11.680 --> 00:08:15.840
and a more recent study found
no significant differences at all

00:08:15.840 --> 00:08:19.840
in brain nor muscle levels between
a young group (average age 21)

00:08:19.840 --> 00:08:23.560
and an older group
(average age 69).

00:08:23.560 --> 00:08:27.920
A study of skin samples found a greater
than 50% drop in young adults

00:08:27.920 --> 00:08:29.440
compared to the skin of newborns,

00:08:30.000 --> 00:08:34.080
and a further drop of about 60%
from young adults to middle age.

00:08:34.080 --> 00:08:38.400
However, there did not seem to be
a further decline from middle to old age.

00:08:38.400 --> 00:08:41.640
There was a small study that found
the NAD+ levels in the liver samples

00:08:41.640 --> 00:08:44.920
of six older individuals
(average age 66)

00:08:44.920 --> 00:08:50.280
was about 30% lower than that of
six younger individuals (average age 39).

00:08:50.280 --> 00:08:53.720
NAD+ levels also may
be lower in macrophage

00:08:53.720 --> 00:08:56.640
white blood cells
in older individuals,

00:08:56.640 --> 00:08:58.920
but in the blood more generally,

00:08:58.920 --> 00:09:01.080
half the studies showed
a decline with age,

00:09:01.080 --> 00:09:02.720
and the other half didn’t.

00:09:02.720 --> 00:09:04.640
By far the largest study

00:09:04.640 --> 00:09:08.720
(enrolling 10 times more people
than the other studies combined)

00:09:08.720 --> 00:09:11.720
found a slight drop in NAD+
in the aging bloodstreams

00:09:11.720 --> 00:09:14.760
of men but no drop in women.

00:09:14.760 --> 00:09:16.240
The bottom line is that,

00:09:16.240 --> 00:09:21.360
given the conflicting results from the
remarkably few studies on the subject,

00:09:21.360 --> 00:09:26.600
it’s misleading to say NAD+
universally decreases with age.

00:09:26.600 --> 00:09:29.560
Regardless, the proof
is in the pudding.

00:09:29.560 --> 00:09:33.040
What about the second premise
that boosting levels late in life

00:09:33.040 --> 00:09:35.200
can improve health and longevity?

00:09:35.200 --> 00:09:43.000
We’ll address that question, next.

00:10:53.640 --> 00:10:56.600
The effects of NAD+ boosters
on aged rodents

00:10:56.600 --> 00:10:58.440
have been described
in the medical literature

00:10:58.440 --> 00:11:02.640
as “profound,” “dramatic”…
“remarkable….”

00:11:02.640 --> 00:11:06.280
Treated mice had increased
physical activity, improved vision,

00:11:06.280 --> 00:11:09.760
and strengthened bones while
delaying or preventing muscle loss,

00:11:09.760 --> 00:11:14.440
hearing loss, cognitive decline,
and ovarian aging.

00:11:14.440 --> 00:11:18.120
Benefits to nearly every organ
system have been documented,

00:11:18.120 --> 00:11:22.360
including improved artery function,
brain function,

00:11:22.360 --> 00:11:25.640
heart function,
immune function,

00:11:25.640 --> 00:11:30.240
kidney function, liver function,
and muscle function.

00:11:30.240 --> 00:11:32.960
For example, a single week of an
NAD+ booster was sufficient

00:11:32.960 --> 00:11:37.280
to restore key markers of muscle
health in a 22-month-old mouse

00:11:37.280 --> 00:11:39.640
to levels similar to that
of a 6-month-old mouse.

00:11:39.640 --> 00:11:42.680
That’s roughly the equivalent
of reverting the muscle health

00:11:42.680 --> 00:11:46.920
of a 70-year-old person back
to when they were just 20.

00:11:46.920 --> 00:11:50.040
NAD+ boosters can also extend
the lifespans of animals,

00:11:50.040 --> 00:11:55.000
presumed to be due to the elevation
of sirtuin activity dependent on NAD+.

00:11:55.000 --> 00:11:56.880
This longevity effect
was first demonstrated

00:11:56.880 --> 00:11:59.520
more than 20 years
ago in yeast cells.

00:11:59.520 --> 00:12:03.440
An overexpression of the genes
involved in NAD+ synthesis

00:12:03.440 --> 00:12:07.320
extended replicative lifespans
by as much as 60%.

00:12:07.320 --> 00:12:09.640
In the microscopic
worm C. elegans,

00:12:09.640 --> 00:12:11.560
NAD+-boosting compounds
have been shown

00:12:11.560 --> 00:12:14.360
to extend lifespans
by up to 16%.

00:12:14.360 --> 00:12:18.200
In mice, one NAD+ booster
was able to extend lifespan

00:12:18.200 --> 00:12:20.480
by a more modest 5%,

00:12:20.480 --> 00:12:23.880
but this was accomplished even when
supplementation was started late in life,

00:12:23.880 --> 00:12:27.040
which is unusual for
longevity treatments.

00:12:27.040 --> 00:12:32.280
No wonder people are excited about
all manner of NAD+ boosting supplements.

00:12:32.280 --> 00:12:35.960
The big question is do any of
these healthspan or lifespan effects

00:12:35.960 --> 00:12:40.080
translate to benefiting humans?

00:12:40.080 --> 00:12:43.760
There are four major NAD+ boosting
supplements on the market these days:

00:12:43.760 --> 00:12:47.080
nicotinic acid (NA),
also known as niacin,

00:12:47.080 --> 00:12:50.640
nicotinamide (NAM),
also known as niacinamide,

00:12:50.640 --> 00:12:53.280
nicotinamide riboside (NR),

00:12:53.280 --> 00:12:56.760
and nicotinamide
mononucleotide (NMN).

00:12:56.760 --> 00:13:01.280
NAD+ can also be given directly,
as well as its hydrogenated form NADH.

00:13:01.280 --> 00:13:04.680
There are also hydrogenated
forms of NMN and NR,

00:13:04.680 --> 00:13:07.640
also known as
dihydronicotinamide riboside.

00:13:07.640 --> 00:13:10.600
So, there is quite
the alphabet soup:

00:13:10.600 --> 00:13:16.880
NA, NAM, NMN, NR, NAD,
NADH, NMNH, and NRH.

00:13:16.880 --> 00:13:18.880
The body can also make
NAD+ “from scratch”

00:13:18.880 --> 00:13:21.880
from the amino
acid tryptophan.

00:13:21.880 --> 00:13:23.400
Given the critical
nature of NAD+,

00:13:23.400 --> 00:13:26.560
it is perhaps unsurprising that the
body has so many different pathways

00:13:26.560 --> 00:13:29.120
utilizing a panoply
of precursors.

00:13:29.760 --> 00:13:32.600
Converting tryptophan to
NAD+ requires eight steps,

00:13:32.600 --> 00:13:37.520
whereas NA, NAM, and NR can be turned
into NAD+ in only two or three steps.

00:13:37.520 --> 00:13:41.000
NMN is a direct
precursor of NAD+,

00:13:41.000 --> 00:13:46.880
but when NMN or NR is taken orally,
it appears to just turn into NA or NAM,

00:13:46.880 --> 00:13:49.440
via rapid degradation
in the bloodstream

00:13:49.440 --> 00:13:51.640
or active conversion in the liver.

00:13:51.640 --> 00:13:54.440
So, why take the more
expensive NMN or NR

00:13:54.440 --> 00:13:56.273
if it’s just going to end
up as NA or NAM?

00:13:56.273 --> 00:14:01.600
Bought in bulk, NA or NAM
would just cost pennies a day

00:14:01.600 --> 00:14:05.160
versus more like a dollar
a day for NR or NMN.

00:14:05.160 --> 00:14:08.600
That would add up to hundreds
of dollars a year for NR or NMN

00:14:08.600 --> 00:14:14.600
compared to closer to only five bucks
for a whole year’s worth of NA or NAM.

00:14:14.600 --> 00:14:20.000
But cost aside, what are the risks
and benefits of all these NAD boosters?

00:14:20.000 --> 00:14:27.760
That’s exactly what I’ll cover, next.

00:15:17.800 --> 00:15:21.880
The name nicotinic acid was
changed to niacin in the 1940s

00:15:21.880 --> 00:15:24.520
to avoid any confusion
with nicotine.

00:15:24.520 --> 00:15:28.680
Either name has to be better
than the original moniker, though:

00:15:28.680 --> 00:15:32.800
vitamin PP
(for pellagra preventing).

00:15:32.800 --> 00:15:36.720
In the 1950s, NA became the world’s
first cholesterol-lowering drug.

00:15:36.720 --> 00:15:40.440
This led to more than 20 trials involving
tens of thousands of individuals

00:15:40.440 --> 00:15:43.920
taking high doses of
NA for up to six years,

00:15:43.920 --> 00:15:47.360
resulting in by far the most
robust safety data we have

00:15:47.360 --> 00:15:49.800
on any of the NAD+ precursors.

00:15:49.800 --> 00:15:53.000
The most striking benefit was found
in the Coronary Drug Project,

00:15:53.000 --> 00:15:56.840
a trial carried out in the pre-statin
drug era of the 1960s and 70s.

00:15:56.840 --> 00:16:00.800
The 15-year follow-up found that
those who had been randomized

00:16:00.800 --> 00:16:06.720
to years of high-dose NA ended up
with a 6.2% drop in absolute mortality

00:16:06.720 --> 00:16:11.800
(52% had died in the NA group
versus 58% in the placebo group).

00:16:11.800 --> 00:16:17.640
This sparked major clinical trials that,
sadly, failed so spectacularly

00:16:17.640 --> 00:16:20.760
that one was even
stopped prematurely.

00:16:20.760 --> 00:16:23.920
All in all, a Cochrane meta-
analysis concluded that

00:16:23.920 --> 00:16:27.800
“no evidence of benefits from
niacin therapy” was found.

00:16:27.800 --> 00:16:30.720
One possible explanation
for the contrasting results

00:16:30.720 --> 00:16:36.240
is that the early promising trials
used immediate release niacin,

00:16:36.240 --> 00:16:40.440
while the newer failed trials
used slow release formulations

00:16:40.440 --> 00:16:43.360
(also known as extended
or sustained release).

00:16:43.360 --> 00:16:48.640
At high doses, regular niacin commonly
causes an intense flushing redness

00:16:48.640 --> 00:16:52.960
and prickly heat sensation similar
to a menopausal hot flash.

00:16:52.960 --> 00:16:56.840
A slow release version was developed
to reduce this flushing reaction,

00:16:56.840 --> 00:17:00.720
catapulting it into a billion-
dollar blockbuster drug,

00:17:00.720 --> 00:17:04.920
but it simply doesn’t work as
well to lower cholesterol.

00:17:04.920 --> 00:17:09.720
The major clinical trial failures led
to the withdrawal of the drug in Europe

00:17:09.720 --> 00:17:12.000
and the removal from
U.S. clinical guidelines

00:17:12.000 --> 00:17:14.600
for cardiovascular
disease prevention.

00:17:14.600 --> 00:17:17.280
There still may be a role
for niacin preparations

00:17:17.280 --> 00:17:18.480
in the treatment
of heart disease

00:17:18.480 --> 00:17:21.280
among patients who cannot
tolerate statin drugs,

00:17:21.280 --> 00:17:25.760
but what about use for the
general public as an NAD+ booster?

00:17:25.760 --> 00:17:28.240
There is a series of
rare genetic defects

00:17:28.240 --> 00:17:31.200
that can lead to a condition
called mitochondrial myopathy

00:17:31.200 --> 00:17:35.240
that’s characterized by low NAD+
levels in the blood and muscles.

00:17:35.240 --> 00:17:39.320
In 2020, researchers demonstrated
that these levels could be repleted

00:17:39.320 --> 00:17:42.520
with 750 to 1,000 mg
a day of NA,

00:17:42.520 --> 00:17:45.760
which led to a significant
improvement in muscle strength.

00:17:45.760 --> 00:17:50.120
This was the first and only study to show
improvements in muscle NAD+ levels

00:17:50.120 --> 00:17:53.320
and performance with
any sort of NAD+ booster.

00:17:53.320 --> 00:17:57.080
In a control group of individuals
without the genetic defect,

00:17:57.080 --> 00:17:59.280
blood levels of NAD+
were raised by NA,

00:17:59.280 --> 00:18:01.400
but not muscle levels,

00:18:01.400 --> 00:18:05.640
suggesting that NAD+ levels are
already “topped off” in normal muscles.

00:18:05.640 --> 00:18:10.560
As you’ll see, this is a recurring
theme among NAD+ boosters.

00:18:10.560 --> 00:18:14.160
We know that large doses of NA
can boost NAD+ levels in human blood,

00:18:14.160 --> 00:18:19.320
but a corresponding increase in sirtuin
activity has yet to be demonstrated.

00:18:19.320 --> 00:18:21.160
Why not give it a try?

00:18:21.160 --> 00:18:25.680
Because of the side effects unearthed
in the cholesterol-lowering trials.

00:18:25.680 --> 00:18:30.840
NA raises blood sugars and may increase
your risk of developing diabetes.

00:18:30.840 --> 00:18:34.000
Based on studies of tens of thousands
of people on high-dose NA

00:18:34.000 --> 00:18:35.760
who were followed for years,

00:18:35.760 --> 00:18:39.920
one would expect that 1 in 43
people taking NA for five years

00:18:39.920 --> 00:18:43.520
would develop diabetes who
otherwise wouldn’t have.

00:18:43.520 --> 00:18:47.800
It’s unclear if this risk is only limited
to slow release formulations.

00:18:47.800 --> 00:18:52.400
The safety buffer, the ratio between
the tolerable upper limit and the RDA,

00:18:52.400 --> 00:18:57.040
is the lowest for NA compared to
half a dozen other common vitamins.

00:18:57.040 --> 00:19:00.120
However, the upper limit is just
based on the flushing reaction,

00:19:00.120 --> 00:19:02.640
which although uncomfortable,
is considered harmless

00:19:02.640 --> 00:19:05.400
and tends to dissipate over time.

00:19:05.400 --> 00:19:08.480
Long-term use can have other
adverse consequences, though,

00:19:08.480 --> 00:19:10.920
including stomach ulcers,
vomiting, abdominal pain,

00:19:10.920 --> 00:19:14.200
diarrhea, and jaundice,
a sign of liver toxicity,

00:19:14.200 --> 00:19:17.920
which is worse with
slow-release formulations.

00:19:17.920 --> 00:19:21.840
There is also a theoretical concern
that excessive NA intake

00:19:21.840 --> 00:19:25.760
may contribute to the development
of Parkinson’s disease.

00:19:25.760 --> 00:19:29.200
Due to the unpleasant flushing and
risk of more serious side effects,

00:19:29.200 --> 00:19:37.800
interest has moved towards
other NAD+ enhancers.

00:19:37.800 --> 00:20:28.640
Ever since nicotinamide (NAM)&nbsp;

00:20:36.160 --> 00:20:38.320
was also shown to cure pellagra,

00:20:38.320 --> 00:20:46.240
both nicotinic acid, NA, and NAM have been
collectively referred to as niacin or vitamin B3,

00:20:46.240 --> 00:20:48.040
though they are
distinct compounds.

00:20:48.040 --> 00:20:52.720
For example, NAM is not plagued by
the same kind of hot flash reaction.

00:20:52.720 --> 00:20:56.040
(Facial flushing attributed to
niacinamide in some older studies

00:20:56.040 --> 00:21:01.800
was likely due to a less purified
form contaminated with residual NA.)

00:21:01.800 --> 00:21:07.200
The relative capacity of NA versus
NAM to generate NAD+ is unclear.

00:21:07.200 --> 00:21:10.160
Neither has been shown
to boost sirtuin activity,

00:21:10.160 --> 00:21:13.280
but both do extend the
lifespan of C. elegans.

00:21:13.280 --> 00:21:16.520
I couldn’t find any longevity
trials for NA in rodents;

00:21:16.520 --> 00:21:22.000
however, NAM was put to the test
and failed to prolong the lives of mice.

00:21:22.000 --> 00:21:26.400
What clinical effects might
we expect in people?

00:21:26.400 --> 00:21:30.960
Previously, I explored the proven anti-
aging effects for topical nicotinamide

00:21:30.960 --> 00:21:36.320
on the skin and the remarkable ability of
oral nicotinamide to help prevent skin cancer.

00:21:36.320 --> 00:21:39.800
I also noted it failed to
prevent type 1 diabetes,

00:21:39.800 --> 00:21:41.880
despite promising mouse data,

00:21:41.880 --> 00:21:45.200
though it may help preserve
residual function in people

00:21:45.200 --> 00:21:47.200
newly diagnosed with
type 1 diabetes,

00:21:47.200 --> 00:21:51.440
but apparently not enough
to affect blood sugar control.

00:21:51.440 --> 00:21:54.640
What about its use
as a NAD+ booster?

00:21:54.640 --> 00:21:57.280
In those with
mitochondrial myopathy,

00:21:57.280 --> 00:22:01.880
NA raised muscle NAD+ levels and
improved mitochondrial and muscle function,

00:22:01.880 --> 00:22:06.080
but in healthy individuals,
muscle NAD+ levels didn’t budge.

00:22:06.080 --> 00:22:09.960
However, the average age of individuals
in the control group was 50.

00:22:09.960 --> 00:22:15.240
What about in older adults whose muscle
NAD+ levels might potentially be lower?

00:22:15.240 --> 00:22:20.240
Four NAD+ precursors were tested
in older adults averaging in their 70s:

00:22:20.240 --> 00:22:25.200
tryptophan, NA, NAM, and NR.

00:22:25.200 --> 00:22:29.400
All four failed to improve
muscle strength or function,

00:22:29.400 --> 00:22:31.880
failed to affect mitochondrial function,

00:22:31.880 --> 00:22:36.200
and failed to even nudge
NAD+ levels in their muscles.

00:22:36.200 --> 00:22:39.960
Why not give it a try anyway?
Again, side effects.

00:22:39.960 --> 00:22:44.440
Like NA, high-dose NAM can cause
gastrointestinal disturbances

00:22:44.440 --> 00:22:47.240
and signs of liver toxicity….

00:22:47.240 --> 00:22:51.360
However, NAM may result in more
issues involving methylation.

00:22:51.360 --> 00:22:55.880
The first step in breaking down excess
NAM is to transfer a methyl group to it,

00:22:55.880 --> 00:22:58.080
forming methylnicotinamide.

00:22:58.080 --> 00:23:01.360
Unfortunately,
methylnicotinamide is neurotoxic

00:23:01.360 --> 00:23:03.480
and can cross the
blood-brain barrier.

00:23:03.480 --> 00:23:07.760
This may explain why NAM can exacerbate
Parkinson’s-like symptoms in rats

00:23:07.760 --> 00:23:10.280
and why Parkinson’s patients
have higher levels

00:23:10.280 --> 00:23:12.560
of the NAM-methylating
enzyme in their brains.

00:23:12.560 --> 00:23:15.600
And the same with Alzheimer's
brains for that matter.

00:23:15.600 --> 00:23:20.440
Excess NAM may also deplete
the body’s pool of methyl groups.

00:23:20.440 --> 00:23:23.920
If you read the Epigenetics chapter
in my book How Not to Age,

00:23:23.920 --> 00:23:29.400
you may remember that DNA methylation is
critical for the regulation of gene expression.

00:23:29.400 --> 00:23:32.800
Epigenetic changes caused by
NAM-induced methyl depletion

00:23:32.800 --> 00:23:36.600
have been blamed as the reason
why rats fed megadoses of NAM

00:23:36.600 --> 00:23:40.280
suffer from fatty livers
and swollen kidneys,

00:23:40.280 --> 00:23:44.000
but that was at a human-equivalent dose
far exceeding what people might take.

00:23:44.000 --> 00:23:46.960
Is there any evidence that
more modest NAM supplementation

00:23:46.960 --> 00:23:50.080
might affect methylation in humans?

00:23:50.080 --> 00:23:55.240
Yes, and even with a single
dose as low as 100 mg.

00:23:55.240 --> 00:23:58.880
Methylation also plays a key role in
breaking down fight-or-flight hormones

00:23:58.880 --> 00:24:04.160
like noradrenaline and neurotransmitters
like serotonin and histamine.

00:24:04.160 --> 00:24:08.000
Within hours of a single
100 mg dose of NAM,

00:24:08.000 --> 00:24:11.640
blood levels of all three
become elevated,

00:24:11.640 --> 00:24:15.520
suggesting their metabolism was impaired
by the shunting of methyl groups

00:24:15.520 --> 00:24:17.960
to deal with the excess NAM.

00:24:17.960 --> 00:24:21.160
Also noted was a significant
rise in homocysteine,

00:24:21.160 --> 00:24:23.360
which is a byproduct of
methylation reactions

00:24:23.360 --> 00:24:27.600
and a risk factor for cardiovascular
disease and dementia.

00:24:27.600 --> 00:24:32.720
Another potential problem with NAM
is that it’s a sirtuin inhibitor.

00:24:33.440 --> 00:24:39.000
Wait, I thought the whole purpose of taking
NAD+ precursors is to boost sirtuin activity.

00:24:39.000 --> 00:24:44.400
Sirtuin enzymes use up
NAD+ and spit out NAM.

00:24:44.400 --> 00:24:50.400
This allows the body to recycle the NAM
back into NAD+ for further sirtuin use.

00:24:50.400 --> 00:24:55.480
But it also means the body can use
NAM as part of a negative feedback loop.

00:24:55.480 --> 00:24:58.440
Like a thermostat in the winter
that shuts down the furnace

00:24:58.440 --> 00:24:59.920
when there’s too much heat,

00:24:59.920 --> 00:25:05.760
the body shuts down NAD+ use by
sirtuins when it detects too much NAM.

00:25:05.760 --> 00:25:08.800
NAM pills didn’t exist
when our bodies evolved;

00:25:08.800 --> 00:25:11.040
so, in the wake of a
sudden wave of NAM,

00:25:11.040 --> 00:25:16.160
the body must think its sirtuins are
churning out too much and dials them back.

00:25:16.160 --> 00:25:21.000
Perhaps, this explains why NAM
fails to prolong the lifespans of mice.

00:25:21.000 --> 00:25:25.040
When the sirtuin-suppressing effects of
NAM were first reported 20 years ago,

00:25:25.040 --> 00:25:28.320
the researchers cautioned that
this could potentially lead to

00:25:28.320 --> 00:25:38.840
“deleterious consequences of long-term
nicotinamide therapy in humans.”

00:27:02.600 --> 00:27:08.800
NR and NMN seem to be more promising
NAD+ precursors than NA or NAM,

00:27:08.800 --> 00:27:13.640
since they don’t cause flushing
nor do they directly inhibit sirtuins.

00:27:13.640 --> 00:27:18.200
In mice, NR and NMN both
raised liver NAD+ levels,

00:27:18.200 --> 00:27:22.840
but of the two, only NR significantly
raised NAD+ in the muscles.

00:27:22.840 --> 00:27:28.200
Also, NR is so far the only NAD+ booster
shown to prolong the lifespan of mice.

00:27:28.200 --> 00:27:30.960
There have been at least
10 clinical trials of NR,

00:27:30.960 --> 00:27:36.640
most showing it can boost human
blood levels of NAD+ by up to 168%.

00:27:36.640 --> 00:27:40.600
Note, though, that most doses
used exceeded 300 mg,

00:27:40.600 --> 00:27:42.560
which is the daily dose
approved as safe

00:27:42.560 --> 00:27:47.240
by the U.S. Food and Drug Administration
and European Food Safety Authority.

00:27:47.240 --> 00:27:52.280
At the approved dose, blood NAD+ is
boosted more on the order of 50 to 60%,

00:27:52.280 --> 00:27:58.120
but no dose was found to affect NAD+ levels
in human muscle (compared to placebo).

00:27:58.880 --> 00:28:02.040
The greater preponderance
of human bioavailability

00:28:02.040 --> 00:28:05.120
and safety data for
NR compared to NMN

00:28:05.120 --> 00:28:09.600
has led some to proclaim NR
as the preferred NAD+ precursor.

00:28:09.600 --> 00:28:12.640
And, by some, I mean employees
of a chemical company

00:28:12.640 --> 00:28:15.040
that produces NR for supplements.

00:28:15.040 --> 00:28:18.880
The question after all
of these human NR trials

00:28:18.880 --> 00:28:23.280
is have any of them
shown clinical benefit?

00:28:23.280 --> 00:28:27.760
Sadly, no.
Let’s go through the alphabet.

00:28:27.760 --> 00:28:29.560
After accounting for
multiple testing,

00:28:29.560 --> 00:28:32.200
randomized, double-blind,
placebo-controlled trials of NR

00:28:32.200 --> 00:28:37.920
in middle-aged or older adults failed to find
any significant benefit over placebo

00:28:37.920 --> 00:28:42.560
for artery stiffness or
artery function, BAT activation,

00:28:42.560 --> 00:28:47.520
blood pressure, blood sugar control,
body weight,

00:28:47.520 --> 00:28:52.480
cardiac energy or ejection fraction,
fat burning,

00:28:52.480 --> 00:28:57.200
fatty liver, exercise capacity,
fatigue,

00:28:57.200 --> 00:29:00.840
insulin sensitivity,
metabolic flexibility,

00:29:00.840 --> 00:29:04.560
metabolic health,
metabolic rate,

00:29:04.560 --> 00:29:08.480
mitochondrial function
or biogenesis,

00:29:08.480 --> 00:29:13.000
muscle blood flow, upper
or lower body muscle strength,

00:29:13.000 --> 00:29:16.720
pancreatic function or the
release of metabolic hormones,

00:29:16.720 --> 00:29:22.080
the treatment of Parkinson’s disease
symptoms, or physical performance.

00:29:22.080 --> 00:29:25.480
NR-hawking companies claim
NR is anti-inflammatory,

00:29:25.480 --> 00:29:30.040
but in their own study, only 3 out of 10
markers of inflammation were affected

00:29:30.040 --> 00:29:31.120
compared to placebo,

00:29:31.120 --> 00:29:34.720
and a subsequent independent study
using the same dose for twice as long

00:29:34.720 --> 00:29:38.120
found zero of 12 markers affected.

00:29:38.120 --> 00:29:42.520
Remarkably, the opposite was found for
many of these outcomes in rats and mice.

00:29:42.520 --> 00:29:46.160
In rodents, NR does raise
NAD+ levels in muscle,

00:29:46.160 --> 00:29:49.160
improving insulin sensitivity
and mitochondrial biogenesis,

00:29:49.160 --> 00:29:51.400
and on down much of the list.

00:29:51.400 --> 00:29:57.520
Why does NR work in rodents but
appear to almost entirely flop in people?

00:29:57.520 --> 00:30:00.200
Some have suggested
inadequate dosing.

00:30:00.200 --> 00:30:02.120
The typical dose used
in mouse studies

00:30:02.120 --> 00:30:05.320
Was about twice that used
in many human studies,

00:30:05.320 --> 00:30:09.360
but a double dose has been
tried in people, to no avail.

00:30:09.360 --> 00:30:15.200
Another possibility is sirtuin inhibition by NAM,
the main degradation product of NR.

00:30:15.200 --> 00:30:16.760
In fact, based on mouse studies,

00:30:16.760 --> 00:30:23.200
NR may metabolize in the gut into NAM or
NA before it even makes it in the bloodstream.

00:30:23.200 --> 00:30:24.680
Either way, unlike in mice,

00:30:24.680 --> 00:30:27.720
NR can’t seem to elevate
NAD+ in human muscle;

00:30:27.720 --> 00:30:31.640
so, no wonder there’s no alteration
of human sirtuin activity.

00:30:31.640 --> 00:30:34.040
Maybe that explains
the disparate results.

00:30:34.040 --> 00:30:37.480
In fact, the key NAD+ synthesizing
enzyme in human muscle biopsies

00:30:37.480 --> 00:30:41.120
was actually suppressed
by NR supplementation.

00:30:41.120 --> 00:30:44.760
This doesn’t happen in mice,
but it does in people.

00:30:44.760 --> 00:30:47.920
Presumably this downregulation
is an adaptive response

00:30:47.920 --> 00:30:52.200
to the unnaturally large flood
of NR coming into the system.

00:30:52.200 --> 00:30:55.320
So, what happens when you
stop taking the supplement?

00:30:55.320 --> 00:30:57.920
How quickly does your enzyme
activity bounce back?

00:30:59.400 --> 00:31:03.640
In mice, not only may
their microbiome affect NR,

00:31:03.640 --> 00:31:07.400
but the NR may affect
their microbiome, too.

00:31:07.400 --> 00:31:10.320
Some of the benefits of NR
can then be transferred

00:31:10.320 --> 00:31:13.160
between mice via
fecal transplants.

00:31:13.160 --> 00:31:16.080
So, at least in mice,
some of the benefits of NR

00:31:16.080 --> 00:31:19.560
may be due to modulating
the mouse microbiome.

00:31:19.560 --> 00:31:22.560
The distinct differences between the
gut flora of humans and rodents

00:31:22.560 --> 00:31:27.480
may offer another explanation why
NR works in them, but not us.

00:31:27.480 --> 00:31:32.360
Unlike NAM, supplementation with
NR did not increase homocysteine levels,

00:31:32.360 --> 00:31:37.640
but one study of a combination of NR
plus a resveratrol analogue called pterostilbene

00:31:37.640 --> 00:31:44.000
raised LDL cholesterol high enough to kill
as many as 1 in 40 long-term users.

00:31:44.000 --> 00:31:47.000
However, this effect is presumed
to be due to the pterostilbene,

00:31:47.000 --> 00:31:53.200
as NR alone has not been shown to raise LDL,
whereas pterostilbene has.

00:31:53.200 --> 00:31:57.400
One study did find that NR seems to
cause a small reduction in hematocrit,

00:31:57.400 --> 00:32:01.640
hemoglobin, and platelet count in
people within a week of starting it.

00:32:01.640 --> 00:32:04.040
This shift towards a
more anemic state

00:32:04.040 --> 00:32:09.720
was suggested to account for impaired
exercise performance seen in rats given NR.

00:32:09.720 --> 00:32:14.800
However, the 35% drop in performance
did not reach statistical significance.

00:32:14.800 --> 00:32:19.280
NR did cause a significant increase
in systemic oxidative stress, however,

00:32:19.280 --> 00:32:22.000
and another rodent study
found a worsening of inflammation

00:32:22.000 --> 00:32:24.840
and deterioration of
metabolic health,

00:32:24.840 --> 00:32:28.280
but if positive effects in rodents
don’t translate to people,

00:32:28.280 --> 00:32:32.280
perhaps we shouldn’t expect
that negative ones will either.

00:32:32.280 --> 00:32:34.600
Regulatory authorities
from Australia, Canada,

00:32:34.600 --> 00:32:38.080
Europe, and the United States
have all authorized NR as safe,

00:32:38.080 --> 00:32:43.240
at least up to 300mg a day
(or 230 in pregnant and lactating women).

00:32:43.240 --> 00:33:47.520
But the lack of demonstrable clinical benefit
would seem to preclude NR supplementation.

00:34:03.680 --> 00:34:08.360
Both NR and NMN have been shown
to have beneficial effects in rodents,

00:34:08.360 --> 00:34:10.840
though they haven’t
been tested side-by-side.

00:34:10.840 --> 00:34:13.760
Both precursors raise blood
levels of NAD+ in people

00:34:13.760 --> 00:34:17.560
but similarly haven’t been pitted
head-to-head against one another.

00:34:17.560 --> 00:34:20.480
One potential advantage
of NMN over NR

00:34:20.480 --> 00:34:22.840
is that it may be more
stable in the bloodstream.

00:34:22.840 --> 00:34:27.960
In mouse blood at least, within an hour,
most NR is converted into NAM,

00:34:27.960 --> 00:34:31.200
whereas NMN levels remain steady.

00:34:31.200 --> 00:34:35.760
You could also argue that NMN is better
because it’s a direct precursor of NAD+,

00:34:35.760 --> 00:34:39.320
whereas NR first has
to be converted to NMN;

00:34:39.320 --> 00:34:42.360
so, we might as well just
take NMN in the first place.

00:34:42.360 --> 00:34:46.080
Ironically, the exact opposite
argument can also be made

00:34:46.080 --> 00:34:50.840
based on the inability of NMN to
pass through cell membranes.

00:34:50.840 --> 00:34:55.640
Structurally, NMN is just NR with
a phosphate group attached to it.

00:34:55.640 --> 00:34:59.400
The phosphate charge prevents NMN
from passing in and out of cells;

00:34:59.400 --> 00:35:04.440
so, to get inside a cell, NMN first
has to be converted into NR.

00:35:04.440 --> 00:35:08.880
Then, once inside, the NR can turn
back into NMN and make NAD+.

00:35:08.880 --> 00:35:14.600
So, if NMN first has to be converted
into NR for cell entry, the argument goes,

00:35:14.600 --> 00:35:17.600
maybe you might as well
just take NR to begin with,

00:35:17.600 --> 00:35:20.360
because there’s no
NMN transporter.

00:35:20.360 --> 00:35:21.880
Or is there?

00:35:21.880 --> 00:35:25.960
An NMN transporter was recently
described (at least in mouse intestine);

00:35:25.960 --> 00:35:29.080
so, maybe NMN is
able to skip the NR step

00:35:29.080 --> 00:35:32.480
and pass directly into cells
to make NAD+ after all.

00:35:32.480 --> 00:35:38.520
However, the evidence that such a NMN
transporter exists remains controversial.

00:35:38.520 --> 00:35:42.440
NMN boasts a long list of
rodent healthspan benefits,

00:35:42.440 --> 00:35:47.600
but, unlike NR, has yet to demonstrate
an extension of mammalian lifespan.

00:35:47.600 --> 00:35:49.320
What about in people?

00:35:49.320 --> 00:35:53.680
There have just been a few human
NMN studies published to date.

00:35:53.680 --> 00:35:55.560
One small study of healthy
middle-aged men

00:35:55.560 --> 00:35:59.120
found that various single doses
had no apparent effect

00:35:59.120 --> 00:36:02.000
on any of the measured variables,
including retinal eye function,

00:36:02.000 --> 00:36:04.000
sleep quality, heart rate,
blood pressure,

00:36:04.000 --> 00:36:06.120
oxygenation,
or body temperature.

00:36:06.120 --> 00:36:10.080
A 12-week study of daily NMN supplementation
in middle-aged men and women

00:36:10.080 --> 00:36:14.000
similarly found no significant
effects on any outcome,

00:36:14.000 --> 00:36:16.200
including lean mass,
muscle mass, body fat,

00:36:16.200 --> 00:36:18.960
blood sugars, cholesterol,
or insulin sensitivity.

00:36:18.960 --> 00:36:23.560
NMN did boost blood NAD+ levels,
though they peaked after the first month

00:36:23.560 --> 00:36:25.960
and then trended down
for months two and three;

00:36:25.960 --> 00:36:29.520
so, there may have been an
adaptive drop in NAD+ synthesis

00:36:29.520 --> 00:36:31.720
as was suspected with NR.

00:36:31.720 --> 00:36:37.360
Like NR, NMN also fails to
raise NAD+ in muscle tissue.

00:36:37.360 --> 00:36:39.400
One study evocatively entitled,

00:36:39.400 --> 00:36:44.880
“Nicotinamide Mononucleotide Supplementation
Enhances Aerobic Capacity in Amateur Runners,”

00:36:44.880 --> 00:36:48.320
tested three different doses of
NMN versus placebo for six weeks

00:36:48.320 --> 00:36:51.280
among young and middle-
aged recreational runners.

00:36:51.280 --> 00:36:57.760
Aerobic capacity was increased at one
ventilatory threshold, but not the other.

00:36:57.760 --> 00:37:00.720
No overall benefit for aerobic
capacity or peak power

00:37:00.720 --> 00:37:04.720
or any of another ten measures of
cardiopulmonary function was found.

00:37:04.720 --> 00:37:06.160
If you measure enough things,

00:37:06.160 --> 00:37:08.960
statistical outliers,
both positive and negative ones,

00:37:08.960 --> 00:37:10.640
can just pop up as flukes.

00:37:10.640 --> 00:37:13.280
For example, the researchers
noted significant improvement

00:37:13.280 --> 00:37:16.000
in the single-leg stance test,

00:37:16.000 --> 00:37:20.400
but the NMN had no significant effect on
any of the other physical function tests.

00:37:20.400 --> 00:37:22.120
And upon closer inspection,

00:37:22.120 --> 00:37:26.560
the apparent single-leg balance benefit
was only found in the middle-dose group

00:37:26.560 --> 00:37:28.880
compared to the high-dose group,

00:37:28.880 --> 00:37:33.440
because the high-dose group ended up
doing slightly worse compared to baseline.

00:37:33.440 --> 00:37:37.920
No significant effect was found for
any of the doses compared to placebo.

00:37:37.920 --> 00:37:43.160
A similar issue can be found in a 12-week
study of NMN supplementation in older adults.

00:37:43.160 --> 00:37:46.400
The NMN company-funded
authors concluded

00:37:46.400 --> 00:37:51.760
that NMN “improved lower limb function
and reduced drowsiness in older adults.”

00:37:51.760 --> 00:37:55.160
But it failed to significantly
affect 16 additional measures,

00:37:55.160 --> 00:37:59.280
including other tests of lower
limb function and fatigue.

00:37:59.280 --> 00:38:04.960
There are so few NMN studies that this
kind of shotgun approach is understandable,

00:38:04.960 --> 00:38:08.560
casting the widest possible net
for effects to be further tested,

00:38:08.560 --> 00:38:13.800
but on their own cannot be presented
as convincing proof of efficacy.

00:38:13.800 --> 00:38:17.520
All of the above NMN studies
were on healthy individuals.

00:38:17.520 --> 00:38:22.120
What about testing NMN on those who
are already metabolically compromised?

00:38:22.120 --> 00:38:24.960
Overweight or obese postmenopausal
women with prediabetes

00:38:24.960 --> 00:38:28.720
were randomized to NMN
or placebo for 10 weeks.

00:38:28.720 --> 00:38:32.240
NMN didn’t seem to affect
body weight or composition,

00:38:32.240 --> 00:38:35.200
liver fat, blood pressure,
or a dozen other metabolic variables,

00:38:35.200 --> 00:38:38.480
but it did improve
muscle insulin sensitivity,

00:38:38.480 --> 00:38:44.240
though not enough to affect insulin levels
or short- or long-term blood sugar control.

00:38:44.240 --> 00:38:49.920
This may be because insulin sensitivity
in the liver and body fat remained unchanged.

00:38:49.920 --> 00:38:53.360
NMN also appeared to have no
effect on mitochondrial function

00:38:53.360 --> 00:38:57.120
or muscle strength,
fatigability, or recovery.

00:38:57.120 --> 00:39:02.640
In terms of safety, NMN shills speak of it as
being naturally found in fruits and vegetables,

00:39:02.640 --> 00:39:06.680
but even the most concentrated sources
(edamame, avocado, and broccoli)

00:39:06.680 --> 00:39:13.040
have over a hundred times less per serving
than the typical NMN supplement dose.

00:39:13.040 --> 00:39:17.840
The same could be said for NR in milk
(human and otherwise).

00:39:17.840 --> 00:39:23.200
There are safety evaluations for NMN
on rats and dogs, but unlike NR,

00:39:23.200 --> 00:39:29.920
supplemental doses of NMN have yet to
be shown as safe for human consumption.

00:39:29.920 --> 00:39:32.360
There are rodent studies
showing that NMN

00:39:32.360 --> 00:39:35.800
may have negative metabolic
consequences compared to placebo,

00:39:35.800 --> 00:39:40.640
but the most serious concern
is nerve degeneration.

00:39:40.640 --> 00:39:44.640
The accumulation of NMN
in nerve cells is toxic.

00:39:44.640 --> 00:39:47.320
Since NR is converted into NMN,

00:39:47.320 --> 00:39:51.360
this is a major concern for
NR supplementation as well.

00:39:51.360 --> 00:39:54.400
The type of nerve damage,
axon degeneration,

00:39:54.400 --> 00:39:58.920
is a major contributor to a variety
of neurodegenerative disorders.

00:39:58.920 --> 00:40:04.880
Blocking an NMN-synthesizing enzyme
appeared to help damaged neurons in vitro,

00:40:04.880 --> 00:40:08.360
protection that’s abolished
by adding NMN back,

00:40:08.360 --> 00:40:12.840
and adding an enzyme that chews up
NMN was also found to be protective,

00:40:12.840 --> 00:40:18.480
further supporting a theory of degenerative
effects of accumulating NMN.

00:40:18.480 --> 00:40:21.600
However, clinical effects
remain theoretical,

00:40:21.600 --> 00:40:27.040
as these adverse effects have only been
demonstrated in fish, mice, and petri dishes.

00:40:27.040 --> 00:40:31.640
Of course, NMN supplements may not
even have NMN in the first place.

00:40:31.640 --> 00:40:36.400
ChromaDex, which sells the rival
supplement Tru Niagen (a form of NR),

00:40:36.400 --> 00:40:41.600
claims to have tested the 22 NMN brands
with the highest market share on Amazon

00:40:41.600 --> 00:40:45.440
and found that most had
virtually no NMN at all.

00:40:45.440 --> 00:40:49.640
Ironically, many of the apparently fake
NMN products displayed quote-unquote

00:40:49.640 --> 00:40:54.600
“certificates of analysis” and carried
hundreds or thousands of positive reviews.

00:40:54.600 --> 00:41:01.920
Evidently, only 3 out of 22 were found to contain
as much NMN as advertised on their label.

00:41:01.920 --> 00:41:04.960
Of course, ChromaDex isn’t
above being shady itself;

00:41:04.960 --> 00:41:08.120
it’s been accused of making
hyped false claims for Tru Niagen

00:41:08.120 --> 00:41:11.920
by both the FDA and the
Better Business Bureau.

00:41:11.920 --> 00:41:17.000
In short, NR has been demonstrated
to be relatively safe but not effective,

00:41:17.000 --> 00:41:26.080
and neither safety nor efficacy
has been established for NMN.

00:42:10.640 --> 00:42:14.080
Taking niacin,
also called nicotinic acid,

00:42:14.080 --> 00:42:16.240
would be about 50 times
more efficient

00:42:16.240 --> 00:42:18.720
than taking
the amino acid tryptophan

00:42:18.720 --> 00:42:19.920
to boost NAD+,

00:42:19.920 --> 00:42:21.720
because only about two percent
of tryptophan

00:42:21.720 --> 00:42:24.040
is converted into niacin.

00:42:24.040 --> 00:42:25.720
Also, tryptophan didn't work

00:42:25.720 --> 00:42:28.120
to improve mitochondrial
or muscle function

00:42:28.120 --> 00:42:30.640
in physically compromised
older adults,

00:42:30.640 --> 00:42:33.720
even when combined
with niacin or nicotinamide.

00:42:33.720 --> 00:42:35.520
And side effects
of taking tryptophan

00:42:35.520 --> 00:42:37.800
include belching and gas,
blurred vision,

00:42:37.800 --> 00:42:40.520
diarrhea, dizziness,
drowsiness, dry mouth,

00:42:40.520 --> 00:42:41.080
headache, heartburn,

00:42:41.080 --> 00:42:43.840
and potentially
a life-threatening condition

00:42:43.840 --> 00:42:47.880
known as eosinophilia-myalgia
syndrome, or EMS.

00:42:47.880 --> 00:42:51.600
There was an epidemic of EMS
tied to tryptophan supplements

00:42:51.600 --> 00:42:54.320
from a single supplier
back in 1989

00:42:54.320 --> 00:42:55.560
that led to their removal

00:42:55.560 --> 00:42:58.880
from the market
for about 15 years.

00:42:58.880 --> 00:43:01.360
Some sort of contaminant
was suspected,

00:43:01.360 --> 00:43:03.240
but the cause
remains a mystery.

00:43:03.240 --> 00:43:04.960
To this day,
tryptophan supplements

00:43:04.960 --> 00:43:07.800
continue to be tainted
with impurities,

00:43:07.800 --> 00:43:10.000
with at least one case
of EMS reported

00:43:10.000 --> 00:43:12.560
decades after
the initial epidemic.

00:43:12.560 --> 00:43:15.720
A case of EMS tied to
a bizarre weight loss diet

00:43:15.720 --> 00:43:18.600
involving hundreds of cups
(~48 L) of cashews,

00:43:18.600 --> 00:43:20.440
a rich source of tryptophan,

00:43:20.440 --> 00:43:22.000
suggests the syndrome
can be caused

00:43:22.000 --> 00:43:25.000
by excess tryptophan directly.

00:43:25.000 --> 00:43:26.040
If anything,

00:43:26.040 --> 00:43:29.520
tryptophan restriction
may be beneficial.

00:43:29.520 --> 00:43:30.480
Nearly 50 years ago,

00:43:30.480 --> 00:43:32.520
it was demonstrated
that restricting

00:43:32.520 --> 00:43:35.160
dietary tryptophan
reduced cancer rates

00:43:35.160 --> 00:43:37.160
and increased
the lifespans of rats

00:43:37.160 --> 00:43:39.320
and, subsequently, mice.

00:43:39.320 --> 00:43:41.280
Vegetarians and vegans
both appear to have

00:43:41.280 --> 00:43:43.760
significantly lower intakes
of tryptophan,

00:43:43.760 --> 00:43:46.240
but only in vegans
does this translate

00:43:46.240 --> 00:43:48.360
to lower
tryptophan blood levels,

00:43:48.360 --> 00:43:49.720
though presumably not

00:43:49.720 --> 00:43:53.360
if they were to take
tryptophan supplements.

00:43:53.360 --> 00:43:56.160
What about taking NAD+ directly?

00:43:56.160 --> 00:43:57.640
This isn't practical

00:43:57.640 --> 00:44:00.440
because of instability
and poor bioavailability.

00:44:00.440 --> 00:44:04.240
NAD+ is vulnerable to heat,
pH, light, and oxygen,

00:44:04.240 --> 00:44:06.600
requiring dark desiccant storage

00:44:06.600 --> 00:44:10.120
at ideally 20 degrees (-29°C)
below freezing.

00:44:10.120 --> 00:44:12.520
NAD+ can be given intravenously,

00:44:12.520 --> 00:44:14.360
a practice started
in the 1950s

00:44:14.360 --> 00:44:17.360
as an "underground" treatment
for alcoholism,

00:44:17.360 --> 00:44:18.880
but when taken orally,

00:44:18.880 --> 00:44:21.520
NAD may be broken down
in the alkaline environment

00:44:21.520 --> 00:44:24.200
of the small intestine,
and NADH,

00:44:24.200 --> 00:44:26.280
the so-called "reduced" form
of NAD+,

00:44:26.280 --> 00:44:28.600
is broken down
in the acidic conditions

00:44:28.600 --> 00:44:29.880
of the stomach.

00:44:29.880 --> 00:44:33.160
(In organic chemistry,
the gain of a hydrogen atom

00:44:33.160 --> 00:44:35.440
is said to quote-unquote
"reduce" the molecule,

00:44:35.440 --> 00:44:39.880
so NADH
is the reduced form of NAD+).

00:44:39.880 --> 00:44:42.720
Enteric forms of NAD+
could potentially survive

00:44:42.720 --> 00:44:45.960
the digestive tract, but,
with the exception of neurons,

00:44:45.960 --> 00:44:49.480
NAD can't cross
into mammalian cells.

00:44:49.480 --> 00:44:52.120
This is why
NAD+ precursor supplements,

00:44:52.120 --> 00:44:55.480
like NMN and NR,
were developed.

00:44:55.480 --> 00:44:57.960
Also, there are evidently
(unpublished) data

00:44:57.960 --> 00:44:59.160
showing that straight NAD+

00:44:59.160 --> 00:45:02.520
can cause severe hyperglycemia
in mice.

00:45:02.520 --> 00:45:04.680
Has it been tested in people?

00:45:04.680 --> 00:45:06.480
NAD+ boosting supplements

00:45:06.480 --> 00:45:08.160
have been found
to improve the learning

00:45:08.160 --> 00:45:11.000
and memory of rodent models
of Alzheimer's disease

00:45:11.000 --> 00:45:12.360
in the lab.

00:45:12.360 --> 00:45:16.720
In 1995, case reports
of apparent benefit of NADH

00:45:16.720 --> 00:45:18.920
for Alzheimer's disease
were published.

00:45:18.920 --> 00:45:22.440
By the next year, an open-label
pilot study was published,

00:45:22.440 --> 00:45:24.600
suggesting it had
a protective effect,

00:45:24.600 --> 00:45:26.600
but without
a placebo control group,

00:45:26.600 --> 00:45:28.320
the only conclusion
that could be drawn

00:45:28.320 --> 00:45:30.200
was to study it further,

00:45:30.200 --> 00:45:31.760
especially since
a similar study

00:45:31.760 --> 00:45:32.840
with the same dose

00:45:32.840 --> 00:45:34.560
over approximately
the same period

00:45:34.560 --> 00:45:38.360
found no evidence
of any cognitive effects.

00:45:38.360 --> 00:45:41.240
There have been
two randomized, double-blind,

00:45:41.240 --> 00:45:42.480
placebo-controlled trials

00:45:42.480 --> 00:45:45.000
of NAD precursors
for Alzheimer's.

00:45:45.000 --> 00:45:47.960
One found no benefit
for memory, attention,

00:45:47.960 --> 00:45:50.600
or clinician ratings
of dementia severity,

00:45:50.600 --> 00:45:52.560
but did maybe find
less of a drop

00:45:52.560 --> 00:45:54.400
in one dementia rating scale

00:45:54.400 --> 00:45:56.920
after six months
of 10 milligrams a day of NADH.

00:45:57.760 --> 00:46:00.240
The other, a six-month study
of nicotinamide,

00:46:00.240 --> 00:46:03.520
failed to find
any clinical effects.

00:46:03.520 --> 00:46:06.720
What about trying
NMNH and NRH,

00:46:06.720 --> 00:46:09.880
the reduced forms
of NMN and NR?

00:46:09.880 --> 00:46:12.560
They both appear
to boost NAD+ higher

00:46:12.560 --> 00:46:14.480
than their
non-reduced counterparts.

00:46:14.480 --> 00:46:17.880
In vitro,
NMNH can raise NAD+ levels

00:46:17.880 --> 00:46:20.440
up to 10 times higher than NMN,

00:46:20.440 --> 00:46:24.720
and NRH (also known as
dihydronicotinamide riboside)

00:46:24.720 --> 00:46:28.520
is up to about 50 times
more potent than NR.

00:46:28.520 --> 00:46:31.400
There are concerns
about stability of NRH

00:46:31.400 --> 00:46:32.440
outside the body,

00:46:32.440 --> 00:46:34.680
since it's sensitive to oxygen
and moisture,

00:46:34.680 --> 00:46:36.000
but within the body,

00:46:36.000 --> 00:46:37.760
NRH may be more stable,

00:46:37.760 --> 00:46:40.120
not rapidly devolving
into nicotinamide,

00:46:40.120 --> 00:46:42.880
like NR does
(at least in mouse blood).

00:46:42.880 --> 00:46:44.480
However, unlike NR,

00:46:44.480 --> 00:46:46.360
NRH does not appear
to be able

00:46:46.360 --> 00:46:50.360
to significantly increase levels
in mouse muscles.

00:46:50.360 --> 00:46:53.240
NRH is said to have
a "spectacular potency"

00:46:53.240 --> 00:46:54.960
for increasing NAD+ levels,

00:46:54.960 --> 00:46:58.400
perhaps the most potent
precursor discovered to date.

00:46:58.400 --> 00:47:01.040
This may not necessarily be
a good thing.

00:47:01.040 --> 00:47:03.640
The extreme boost
afforded by NRH

00:47:03.640 --> 00:47:07.440
had detrimental consequences
in human liver cells in vitro,

00:47:07.440 --> 00:47:09.600
resulting from
an excessive accumulation

00:47:09.600 --> 00:47:10.920
of free radicals.

00:47:10.920 --> 00:47:12.000
In addition to oxidation,

00:47:12.000 --> 00:47:15.200
NRH was also found
promote inflammation.

00:47:15.200 --> 00:47:17.400
Pro-inflammatory effects
were noted for NRH

00:47:17.400 --> 00:47:22.800
on human immune cells in vitro
(but not for NMN, NAM, or NR).

00:47:22.800 --> 00:47:26.040
Because it appears that NMNH
is converted to NRH

00:47:26.040 --> 00:47:26.840
to enter cells,

00:47:27.520 --> 00:47:29.480
these potentially
deleterious effects

00:47:29.480 --> 00:47:31.880
may be shared
by NMNH as well

00:47:31.880 --> 00:47:37.640
(though this has yet
to be tested).

00:48:47.400 --> 00:48:48.880
Most of the reported
side effects

00:48:48.880 --> 00:48:53.320
for NAD+ precursors,
like NAM, NR, and NMN,

00:48:53.320 --> 00:48:55.200
are relatively rare and minor,

00:48:55.200 --> 00:48:58.000
for example, diarrhea,
nausea, rashes, hot flashes,

00:48:58.000 --> 00:48:59.440
and leg cramps.

00:48:59.440 --> 00:49:02.960
Both NR and NMN
raise NAM levels,

00:49:02.960 --> 00:49:05.800
so may share
in the same concerns

00:49:05.800 --> 00:49:09.440
regarding sirtuin inhibition,
methyl depletion,

00:49:09.440 --> 00:49:13.960
and potential adverse effects
of NAM breakdown products.

00:49:13.960 --> 00:49:16.800
Another theoretical concern
of NAD+ boosting

00:49:16.800 --> 00:49:18.640
is the exacerbation
of infections

00:49:18.640 --> 00:49:21.040
by a group of bacteria
called Haemophilus

00:49:21.040 --> 00:49:23.560
(from the Greek
meaning "blood loving,"

00:49:23.560 --> 00:49:25.760
though can also cause
infections of the lungs,

00:49:25.760 --> 00:49:28.520
brain, throat,
flesh, and joints).

00:49:28.520 --> 00:49:31.920
Haemophilus bacteria lack
the ability to make NAD+,

00:49:31.920 --> 00:49:33.800
so rely on host levels,

00:49:33.800 --> 00:49:36.200
raising the possibility
that higher blood levels

00:49:36.200 --> 00:49:39.960
might worsen the disease course
of infected individuals.

00:49:39.960 --> 00:49:42.160
Ironically,
elevated NAD+ levels

00:49:42.160 --> 00:49:45.240
may also fuel
immune system overreaction

00:49:45.240 --> 00:49:48.840
in cases of auto-immune
and inflammatory disease.

00:49:48.840 --> 00:49:52.280
When fully activated,
the immune system is voracious.

00:49:52.280 --> 00:49:54.280
The immune reaction
to a blood infection

00:49:54.280 --> 00:49:58.320
or extensive burns can burn
4,000 calories a day,

00:49:58.320 --> 00:50:01.400
approximating military training
in the Arctic.

00:50:01.400 --> 00:50:04.080
Since NAD+ is used by cells
to produce energy,

00:50:04.080 --> 00:50:05.520
it's no surprise that we find

00:50:05.520 --> 00:50:08.640
the primary NAD+
synthesizing enzyme

00:50:08.640 --> 00:50:10.080
strongly upregulated

00:50:10.080 --> 00:50:12.360
in tissues
that are actively inflamed.

00:50:12.360 --> 00:50:16.120
For example,
the enzyme NAMPT is elevated

00:50:16.120 --> 00:50:19.640
in colonoscopy biopsies
taken from inflamed areas

00:50:19.640 --> 00:50:22.520
in patients with
inflammatory bowel disease,

00:50:22.520 --> 00:50:24.720
and higher levels
are correlated

00:50:24.720 --> 00:50:27.000
with greater disease severity.

00:50:27.000 --> 00:50:30.560
So, for those suffering from
chronic autoimmune diseases,

00:50:30.560 --> 00:50:32.520
such as rheumatoid arthritis,

00:50:32.520 --> 00:50:34.680
NAD+ boosting
could potentially have

00:50:34.680 --> 00:50:37.320
a "profound negative impact."

00:50:37.320 --> 00:50:40.280
This explains
why tamping down NAD+

00:50:40.280 --> 00:50:43.440
with NAMPT inhibitors
has been shown

00:50:43.440 --> 00:50:47.080
to ameliorate colitis
and arthritis in mice,

00:50:47.080 --> 00:50:49.600
but this has yet
to be tested in people.

00:50:49.600 --> 00:50:52.320
Such NAD+ depleting drugs
have, however,

00:50:52.320 --> 00:50:55.000
been used in cancer patients.

00:50:55.000 --> 00:50:59.040
Malignancy is another heavily
energy-consuming process.

00:50:59.040 --> 00:51:02.360
NAD+ may, therefore,
have a tumor-promoting effect

00:51:02.360 --> 00:51:04.760
by promoting cancer cell growth
and spread.

00:51:04.760 --> 00:51:08.280
For example, NAMPT,
the NAD+-forming enzyme,

00:51:08.280 --> 00:51:10.640
is highly expressed
in cancerous brain tumors

00:51:10.640 --> 00:51:14.320
and correlates with
decreased patient survival.

00:51:14.320 --> 00:51:17.560
This has led to attempts
to use NAD+-depleting therapies

00:51:17.560 --> 00:51:20.760
to try to starve
cancer progression,

00:51:20.760 --> 00:51:23.520
but this approach is confounded
by rapid onset injury

00:51:23.520 --> 00:51:25.840
to another
energy-intensive tissue,

00:51:25.840 --> 00:51:29.960
the retina,
risking blindness.

00:51:29.960 --> 00:51:32.800
Giving NMN to mice
with pancreatic cancer

00:51:32.800 --> 00:51:35.400
accelerates the progression
of the cancer,

00:51:35.400 --> 00:51:38.200
thought due to the aggravation
of inflammation.

00:51:38.200 --> 00:51:41.440
The researchers conclude that
consumers of NAD+ supplements

00:51:41.440 --> 00:51:44.560
must "balance the advantageous
anti-ageing effects

00:51:44.560 --> 00:51:49.240
with the potential detrimental
pro-tumorigenic side effects."

00:51:49.240 --> 00:51:51.920
Perhaps this explains
why the best NAD+ boosters

00:51:51.920 --> 00:51:53.360
have ever been able to do

00:51:53.360 --> 00:51:57.000
is increase mice lifespan
by five percent.

00:51:57.000 --> 00:51:58.600
On the other hand,
as you'll remember,

00:51:58.600 --> 00:52:02.280
NAM successfully prevented
human skin cancers

00:52:02.280 --> 00:52:04.360
and has been found
to reduce the incidence

00:52:04.360 --> 00:52:06.800
of a variety
of carcinogen-induced tumors

00:52:06.800 --> 00:52:08.120
in rodents.

00:52:08.120 --> 00:52:10.520
The disparate results
may in part be due

00:52:10.520 --> 00:52:13.080
to the disparate impact
sirtuin activation

00:52:13.080 --> 00:52:15.200
may have on different cancers.

00:52:15.200 --> 00:52:16.840
Sirtuin activity
can be overexpressed

00:52:16.840 --> 00:52:18.240
in some cancers

00:52:18.240 --> 00:52:21.200
(like thyroid carcinomas
and lung metastasis)

00:52:21.200 --> 00:52:22.520
but reduced in others

00:52:22.520 --> 00:52:25.080
(like brain, bladder, prostate,
and ovarian tumors).

00:52:25.080 --> 00:52:28.240
The bottom line
is that particular caution

00:52:28.240 --> 00:52:30.800
should be used
for NAD+-boosting supplements

00:52:30.800 --> 00:52:32.200
by those with cancer,

00:52:32.200 --> 00:52:35.160
or a personal or strong
family history of cancer,

00:52:35.160 --> 00:52:38.000
and perhaps also by those
with inflammatory disorders

00:52:38.000 --> 00:52:45.240
and certain active infections.

00:54:00.160 --> 00:54:04.040
So, which NAD+ boosting
supplement is best?

00:54:04.040 --> 00:54:05.760
There’s no clear standout,

00:54:05.760 --> 00:54:08.560
as hardly any of the preclinical
effects found in the lab

00:54:08.560 --> 00:54:12.680
have translated into evidence
of human clinical benefit.

00:54:12.680 --> 00:54:17.960
Perhaps, this failure is to be expected
given the complexity of NAD+ physiology,

00:54:17.960 --> 00:54:23.240
with its juggling of multiple precursors,
production pathways, and recycling routes.

00:54:23.240 --> 00:54:27.440
The bottom line is that it’s just too early
to say if NAD+ booster supplementation

00:54:27.440 --> 00:54:31.040
will ever live up to even
a fraction of the hype.

00:54:31.040 --> 00:54:36.480
Many more, larger, and longer-term studies
are necessary to establish safety and efficacy.

00:54:36.480 --> 00:54:42.640
The problem is that because NA, NAM,
NR, and NMN are all natural products,

00:54:42.640 --> 00:54:44.160
they can’t be patented;

00:54:44.160 --> 00:54:48.400
so, the money for well-designed
clinical trials is not as available.

00:54:48.400 --> 00:54:52.760
The reason there have been comparatively
more trials done on NR than NMN

00:54:52.760 --> 00:55:00.000
is that patents were originally issued for NR
before being invalidated as unpatentable.

00:55:00.000 --> 00:55:04.040
Perhaps blindly overloading the
system with NAD+ precursors

00:55:04.040 --> 00:55:07.560
is not the best way to go
about NAD+ restoration.

00:55:07.560 --> 00:55:13.960
The body seems too smart to allow such
blunt incursion to affect tissue levels.

00:55:13.960 --> 00:55:16.800
Maybe these supplements are
just profit-making distractions

00:55:16.800 --> 00:55:20.360
from more natural approaches.

00:55:20.360 --> 00:55:25.400
Broadly, there are three main
ways to increase NAD+ levels.

00:55:25.400 --> 00:55:29.480
Increasing the supply of NAD+
precursors is just the first.

00:55:29.480 --> 00:55:32.520
The other two are having
the body make more,

00:55:32.520 --> 00:55:35.000
by activating NAD+
synthesizing enzymes,

00:55:35.000 --> 00:55:41.440
or have the body use less, via an
inhibition of excess NAD+ degradation.

00:55:41.440 --> 00:55:47.720
The primary determinant of NAD+
synthesis in the enzyme NAMPT.

00:55:47.720 --> 00:55:52.160
An abundance of NAMPT tends to
decrease with age in human muscle,

00:55:52.160 --> 00:55:56.280
dropping steadily by about 40%
between the ages of 20 and 80.

00:55:56.280 --> 00:55:58.720
In our liver, it drops by half.

00:55:58.720 --> 00:56:01.880
However, age-related diseases,
such as atherosclerosis,

00:56:01.880 --> 00:56:03.600
cancer, diabetes,
and rheumatoid arthritis,

00:56:03.600 --> 00:56:07.320
have been found to exacerbate
NAMPT decline,

00:56:07.320 --> 00:56:09.920
raising a chicken or
the egg question.

00:56:09.920 --> 00:56:13.200
There’s where interventional
trials come in.

00:56:13.200 --> 00:56:17.880
Similar NAMPT declines have been
noted in aging rats and mice.

00:56:17.880 --> 00:56:20.640
Does boosting NAMPT help?

00:56:20.640 --> 00:56:24.800
Increasing NAMPT or its species
equivalent increases the lifespans

00:56:24.800 --> 00:56:28.200
of yeast, fruit flies, and rodents.

00:56:28.200 --> 00:56:33.920
An NAMPT boost also increases aerobic
capacity and exercise endurance in mice,

00:56:33.920 --> 00:56:36.920
in addition to helping them live longer.

00:56:36.920 --> 00:56:41.640
Enhanced expression of NAMPT increases
the NAD+ levels in the muscles in mice

00:56:41.640 --> 00:56:45.960
comparable to feeding them
dietary NAD+ precursors,

00:56:45.960 --> 00:56:46.680
but if you remember,

00:56:46.680 --> 00:56:51.760
NAD+ precursors don’t seem to be able to
affect NAD+ muscle levels in most people.

00:56:51.760 --> 00:56:55.280
In fact, such supplements can
actually suppress NAMPT,

00:56:55.280 --> 00:56:59.720
while boosting that methylating enzyme
to rid the body of the excess.

00:56:59.720 --> 00:57:01.720
In addition to methyl depletion,

00:57:01.720 --> 00:57:03.600
chronic administration
of these supplements

00:57:03.600 --> 00:57:07.720
could potentially then leave people
worse off should they ever stop them.

00:57:07.720 --> 00:57:12.600
There is, however, a way to naturally
boost NAMPT and NAD+ levels in humans

00:57:12.600 --> 00:57:16.600
without any supplements: exercise.

00:57:16.600 --> 00:57:20.480
Athletes have about twice the NAMPT
expression in their musculature

00:57:20.480 --> 00:57:22.760
compared to sedentary individuals.

00:57:22.760 --> 00:57:24.680
To prove cause and effect,

00:57:24.680 --> 00:57:29.320
sedentary men and women started
a stationary bike exercise protocol,

00:57:29.320 --> 00:57:34.680
and within three weeks, NAMPT
levels increased by 127%.

00:57:34.680 --> 00:57:38.360
Resistance training can
also increase NAMPT,

00:57:38.360 --> 00:57:43.200
and this can also translate into a
127% increase in muscle NAD+ levels

00:57:43.200 --> 00:57:46.000
and a rise in sirtuin activity.

00:57:46.000 --> 00:57:46.920
In other words,

00:57:46.920 --> 00:57:56.120
exercise can do what NAD+
boosting supplements can’t.

00:59:42.200 --> 00:59:45.200
There are three
NAD+ boosting strategies:

00:59:45.200 --> 00:59:48.040
Increasing the supply
of NAD+ precursors

00:59:48.040 --> 00:59:49.280
is just one way.

00:59:49.280 --> 00:59:51.880
The other two
are having the body make more,

00:59:51.880 --> 00:59:54.360
by activating
NAD+-synthesizing enzymes,

00:59:54.360 --> 00:59:57.960
or have the body use less,
by, for example,

00:59:57.960 --> 01:00:00.400
conserving it, by using less.

01:00:00.400 --> 01:00:02.840
Besides sirtuins,
the major consumers

01:00:02.840 --> 01:00:06.680
of NAD+ are PARP-1 and CD38.

01:00:06.680 --> 01:00:11.760
PARP-1 is an enzyme
that uses NAD+ to repair DNA.

01:00:11.760 --> 01:00:13.800
The more oxidative DNA damage,

01:00:13.800 --> 01:00:17.200
the more single
and double stranded DNA breaks,

01:00:17.200 --> 01:00:19.840
the more enzymes like PARP-1
need to be activated

01:00:19.840 --> 01:00:21.760
to come to the rescue.

01:00:21.760 --> 01:00:25.000
This uses up a lot of NAD.

01:00:25.000 --> 01:00:27.240
As DNA damage
accumulates with age,

01:00:27.240 --> 01:00:29.800
the rising need
for repair enzymes like PARP-1

01:00:29.800 --> 01:00:33.480
causes a major drain
on NAD+ levels.

01:00:33.480 --> 01:00:36.560
Exposing cells in vitro
to DNA damaging agents,

01:00:36.560 --> 01:00:39.800
such as gamma radiation
or genotoxic chemicals,

01:00:39.800 --> 01:00:42.160
can cause an 80
to 90 percent drop

01:00:42.160 --> 01:00:45.200
in NAD+ levels
within a matter of minutes.

01:00:45.200 --> 01:00:47.520
This has led to the search
for PARP-1 blockers

01:00:47.520 --> 01:00:49.760
to preserve NAD+ levels,

01:00:49.760 --> 01:00:52.680
but rather than blocking
DNA repair,

01:00:52.680 --> 01:00:54.840
why not work to prevent
so much damage

01:00:54.840 --> 01:00:56.360
in the first place?

01:00:56.360 --> 01:00:58.240
For example,
the severe oxidative stress

01:00:58.240 --> 01:00:59.840
of a high-fat diet

01:00:59.840 --> 01:01:03.960
can lead to PARP-1 activation
and NAD+ depletion in mice,

01:01:03.960 --> 01:01:06.760
but NAD+ levels can be
"dramatically restored"

01:01:06.760 --> 01:01:09.560
by feeding them
"purple sweet potato color,"

01:01:09.560 --> 01:01:11.640
the natural
anthocyanin pigments

01:01:11.640 --> 01:01:14.000
found in purple sweet potatoes.

01:01:14.000 --> 01:01:18.640
Or, of course, you can just not
feed them a high-fat diet.

01:01:18.640 --> 01:01:21.720
DNA repair is a good thing.

01:01:21.720 --> 01:01:23.160
PARP-1 may be
one of the reasons

01:01:23.160 --> 01:01:26.040
NAD+-boosting interventions
can improve healthspans

01:01:26.040 --> 01:01:28.440
and lifespans
in laboratory animals.

01:01:28.440 --> 01:01:31.000
Greater PARP activity
strongly correlates

01:01:31.000 --> 01:01:32.600
with longer lifespan

01:01:32.600 --> 01:01:34.680
across about a dozen
mammalian species,

01:01:34.680 --> 01:01:36.960
and the PARP activity
of human centenarians

01:01:36.960 --> 01:01:40.680
averages 60 percent higher
than younger controls.

01:01:40.680 --> 01:01:44.760
However, persistent activation
can lead to NAD+ depletion,

01:01:44.760 --> 01:01:47.400
and overactivation
can lead to cell death.

01:01:47.400 --> 01:01:52.080
So, we should try to keep
oxidative stress to a minimum.

01:01:52.080 --> 01:01:56.920
CD38 is another major guzzler
of NAD+.

01:01:56.920 --> 01:01:58.680
It's an enzyme that uses NAD+

01:01:58.680 --> 01:02:00.720
found concentrated
on the surfaces

01:02:00.720 --> 01:02:03.160
of immune cells
and robustly induced

01:02:03.160 --> 01:02:06.440
in the context of inflammation.

01:02:06.440 --> 01:02:09.120
The rise of CD38 activity
with age

01:02:09.120 --> 01:02:12.560
has been blamed on persistent
"inflammaging" activation,

01:02:12.560 --> 01:02:16.400
the rise in systemic low-grade
inflammation in our bodies

01:02:16.400 --> 01:02:17.400
when we get older,

01:02:17.400 --> 01:02:21.160
which may be a major culprit
for falling NAD+ levels.

01:02:21.160 --> 01:02:23.680
For example, blocking CD38
has been found

01:02:23.680 --> 01:02:26.080
to raise NAD+ levels
in old mice

01:02:26.080 --> 01:02:28.480
comparable to that
of younger mice.

01:02:28.480 --> 01:02:32.480
So, oxidation and inflammation

01:02:32.480 --> 01:02:34.960
can lead to a drop
in NAD+ levels,

01:02:34.960 --> 01:02:39.720
due to the excess activation
of the NAD+ consuming enzymes.

01:02:39.720 --> 01:02:42.320
This may explain why
protective sirtuin activity

01:02:42.320 --> 01:02:45.280
is reduced in obesity,
a condition characterized

01:02:45.280 --> 01:02:47.960
by oxidative stress
and inflammation.

01:02:47.960 --> 01:02:50.280
A study of identical twin pairs

01:02:50.280 --> 01:02:53.880
in which one, on average,
was obese and the other not,

01:02:53.880 --> 01:02:56.720
found significantly
less sirtuin expression

01:02:56.720 --> 01:02:58.440
in the obese twin,

01:02:58.440 --> 01:03:00.760
despite having
the same genetics.

01:03:00.760 --> 01:03:02.800
And randomize people
to a six-month trial

01:03:02.800 --> 01:03:05.200
of 25 percent
calorie restriction,

01:03:05.200 --> 01:03:07.400
and you can show a boost
in sirtuin expression

01:03:07.400 --> 01:03:11.000
along with a decrease
in DNA damage.

01:03:11.000 --> 01:03:13.120
Protein restriction
may have a similar effect,

01:03:13.120 --> 01:03:15.160
since men and women
with higher protein intake

01:03:15.160 --> 01:03:18.240
tend to have lower levels
of NAD+ in their blood,

01:03:18.240 --> 01:03:20.280
thought to be due
to the oxidative stress

01:03:20.280 --> 01:03:24.040
induced by protein
breakdown byproducts.

01:03:24.040 --> 01:03:26.520
If oxidation and inflammation
are responsible

01:03:26.520 --> 01:03:28.440
for a drop in NAD+ levels,

01:03:28.440 --> 01:03:30.360
then what about the antioxidant

01:03:30.360 --> 01:03:32.640
and anti-inflammatory
phytonutrients

01:03:32.640 --> 01:03:34.480
in healthy plant foods?

01:03:34.480 --> 01:03:37.440
After screening
more than 14,000 compounds,

01:03:37.440 --> 01:03:40.200
almost all flavonoids
were found to be effective

01:03:40.200 --> 01:03:42.720
in a test for CD38 inhibition.

01:03:42.720 --> 01:03:45.520
The two most effective
were cyanidin,

01:03:45.520 --> 01:03:47.960
found in red cabbage
and blackberries,

01:03:47.960 --> 01:03:52.320
and quercetagetin,
found in marigold flower tea.

01:03:52.320 --> 01:03:54.680
Another study found
the three most potent compounds

01:03:54.680 --> 01:03:57.800
were luteolin, kuromanin,
and luteolinidin.

01:03:57.800 --> 01:04:03.000
Luteolin is found concentrated
in oregano, radicchio,

01:04:03.000 --> 01:04:05.560
and chrysanthemum tea.

01:04:05.560 --> 01:04:08.560
Kuromanin is found
in black berries, purple corn,

01:04:08.560 --> 01:04:10.160
and hibiscus tea.

01:04:10.160 --> 01:04:12.640
Corn tortillas are
surprisingly easy to make;

01:04:12.640 --> 01:04:15.400
so why not choose blue
or purple masa

01:04:15.400 --> 01:04:17.320
to make them even healthier?

01:04:17.320 --> 01:04:18.520
Luteolinidin,

01:04:18.520 --> 01:04:20.840
found to increase NAD+
in the hearts of rats,

01:04:20.840 --> 01:04:23.080
can be found in red sorghum,

01:04:23.080 --> 01:04:25.800
one of the components
of my prebiotic BROL mix,

01:04:25.800 --> 01:04:27.680
when I can find it.

01:04:27.680 --> 01:04:29.120
The flavonoid apigenin

01:04:29.120 --> 01:04:31.920
is a well-established
CD38 inhibitor.

01:04:31.920 --> 01:04:35.480
When given to mice,
apigenin boosts NAD+ levels

01:04:35.480 --> 01:04:38.520
by about 50 percent,
which is what people would get

01:04:38.520 --> 01:04:42.400
taking the maximum
tolerable daily dose of NR.

01:04:42.400 --> 01:04:46.960
The best sources are parsley
and chamomile tea.

01:04:46.960 --> 01:04:49.880
A wide range of flavonoids
found in green tea, turmeric,

01:04:49.880 --> 01:04:51.760
and fruits and vegetables
have also been found

01:04:51.760 --> 01:04:55.160
to prevent NAD+ depletion
in human cells in vitro

01:04:55.160 --> 01:04:58.080
at levels found in the blood
after consumption.

01:04:58.080 --> 01:05:01.080
How much do you have to eat,
though?

01:05:01.080 --> 01:05:04.120
Proanthocyanidins have been
found to lower PARP-1

01:05:04.120 --> 01:05:07.360
and CD38 expression in rats.

01:05:07.360 --> 01:05:10.240
NAD+ and sirtuin activity
was significantly boosted

01:05:10.240 --> 01:05:14.720
at the human equivalent dose
of about 280 milligrams a day.

01:05:14.720 --> 01:05:16.440
How much is that?

01:05:16.440 --> 01:05:18.440
That's the amount
of proanthocyanidins

01:05:18.440 --> 01:05:21.680
found in a single apple.

01:05:21.680 --> 01:05:25.200
You could also reach that dose
eating two plums,

01:05:25.200 --> 01:05:27.120
a half cup of wild blueberries,

01:05:27.120 --> 01:05:29.360
a little over a teaspoon
of cinnamon,

01:05:29.360 --> 01:05:31.960
or a little over a tablespoon,
like four teaspoons,

01:05:31.960 --> 01:05:33.280
of cocoa powder.

01:05:33.280 --> 01:05:36.240
Quercetin is another suppressor
of PARP-1 and CD38

01:05:36.240 --> 01:05:39.280
shown to increase
sirtuin activity in mice.

01:05:39.280 --> 01:05:42.320
The concentration necessary
to lower PARP-1 in vitro

01:05:42.320 --> 01:05:45.360
can be achieved by taking
a quercetin supplement,

01:05:45.360 --> 01:05:47.320
but typical supplement
manufacturers'

01:05:47.320 --> 01:05:50.040
recommended doses
are up to 100 times

01:05:50.040 --> 01:05:52.320
the average daily
dietary intake.

01:05:52.320 --> 01:05:55.640
Thankfully, food works too.

01:05:55.640 --> 01:05:57.920
Researchers fried up
one and a half yellow onions

01:05:57.920 --> 01:05:59.440
and raised
quercetin blood levels

01:05:59.440 --> 01:06:01.800
to about 75 percent there.

01:06:01.800 --> 01:06:04.440
And so, two onions might do it.

01:06:04.440 --> 01:06:06.360
There's no long-term
safety data

01:06:06.360 --> 01:06:08.480
on high-dose
flavonoid supplementation;

01:06:08.480 --> 01:06:10.800
so, public health researchers
suggest

01:06:10.800 --> 01:06:13.720
"caution should be exercised
in ingesting them

01:06:13.720 --> 01:06:16.200
at levels above which
would be obtained

01:06:16.200 --> 01:06:23.680
from a typical
vegetarian diet."

